entries.body:
`--allow fs.read=<dir>` and `--allow fs.write=<dir>` now work beside `--sandbox`. Each directory is resolved to its real path at build time and must exist. Landlock then grants the capability beneath those directories only, not beneath `/`, with one exception: a `main` that reaches `process.spawn` keeps read access beneath `/` so that `exec` can load a program.

The command exits 2 for any of these:
- a scope without `--sandbox`;
- a scope in `--deny`;
- a scope of any other capability;
- a directory that does not exist.

At run time, a scope directory that cannot be opened makes strict mode exit 126. Best-effort mode names the directory once and grants nothing beneath it. Strict mode refuses a write scope below Landlock ABI 3.

Refs: docs/wp37-os-sandbox.md
Tests: tests/run.js sandbox, tests/nish/cli.ts checkSandboxScopes
Fixes #451
